# UBSan suppressions for OPEN fuzzing findings, used only when FUZZ_DEFS contains -DFUZZ_SKIP_KNOWN so a long
# run keeps exploring past them. Default fuzzing (and CI without FUZZ_DEFS) reports them. Remove a line when its
# fix lands. Memory-safety findings cannot be suppressed here: the harnesses steer around those instead.
# F1: np.fromfile text mode casts NaN/Inf/out-of-range values to an integer dtype (np_io.c io_store)
float-cast-overflow:io_store
# F6: np.loadtxt / np.genfromtxt memcpy from a NULL buffer when the file yields no values (np_io.c)
nonnull-attribute:r_loadtxt
nonnull-attribute:r_genfromtxt
# F11 (systemic): routines and their helpers cast numeric arguments to int64/int without a range check, e.g.
# (int64_t)args[k].num with NaN/Inf/1e300 (about 140 direct sites, scipy_signal.c the most, plus helpers such as
# fw2_read_hsize). Suppressing the cast itself keeps the x86 result (INT64_MIN) flowing, so any memory error it
# leads to downstream is still reported. This covers every float-cast-overflow while the class is open.
float-cast-overflow:*
